  "sandboxConfig": {
    "note": "Amendment 1 resolves the read-only-vs-build contradiction by relocating every mutating package command to a disposable sandbox (see the standard's Sandbox Execution Contract) instead of weakening or omitting any command category. Every command below is 'sandboxed': true and executes against a hash-verified git-archive extraction of authorizedCandidateHead, never against the real public root. Per AC-03, the real public root and Core are read-only copy sources only and are never live dependency-link targets: every third-party node_modules entry is first physically copied from the real public root's installed store into a dedicated dependency-store subtree of the disposable temporary support directory, then junctioned (directories) or hard-linked (files) from that support-owned copy into the sandbox - never linked directly from either real repository. `next` is a documented exception: it is physically copied straight into the sandbox's own node_modules with no junction step anywhere in its path, because webpack's resolve.symlinks realpaths through any junction (including one targeting a support-owned copy) during module resolution, and only a zero-junction path resolves entirely inside the sandbox.",
